#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to quantum-safe cryptography {#introduction-to-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Pengantar kriptografi quantum-safe {#introduction-to-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since quantum computers represent a [distinct and potentially more powerful "
"paradigm for "
"computing](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-"
"future-of-quantum-computing-with) than the classical computers in use today,"
" cryptographic security needs to be reassessed for a world where quantum "
"computers may <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The rapid or exponential "
"growth, increase, or multiplication of something, typically in a biological,"
" technological, or abstract context.\">proliferate</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"enabling new cryptographic attacks that would not be possible using "
"classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena komputer kuantum mewakili [paradigma komputasi yang berbeda dan "
"berpotensi lebih "
"kuat](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-future-"
"of-quantum-computing-with) daripada komputer klasikal yang digunakan saat "
"ini, keamanan kriptografi perlu dinilai ulang untuk dunia di mana komputer "
"kuantum mungkin <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pertumbuhan, peningkatan, "
"atau perkalian yang cepat atau eksponensial dari sesuatu, biasanya dalam "
"konteks biologis, teknologi, atau abstrak.\">berkembang "
"pesat</DefinitionTooltip>, memungkinkan serangan kriptografi baru yang tidak"
" mungkin dilakukan menggunakan komputer klasikal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These attacks may occur in future on data that is being transmitted or "
"stored now known as *harvest now, decrypt later*, so it is not sufficient to"
" wait until the required systems are available, but to make changes now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Serangan ini mungkin terjadi di masa depan pada data yang sedang "
"ditransmisikan atau disimpan sekarang yang dikenal sebagai *harvest now, "
"decrypt later*, sehingga tidak cukup menunggu sampai sistem yang diperlukan "
"tersedia, tetapi harus melakukan perubahan sekarang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The field of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as Post Quantum or "
"Quantum-Resistant. Cryptographic algorithms, protocols, or systems that are "
"designed to withstand attacks from quantum computers. Even as quantum "
"computing technology progresses, the security of digital communication and "
"sensitive information needs to remains intact.\">**quantum-safe "
"cryptography**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) encompasses efforts to [identify "
"and develop cryptographic "
"schemes](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) that can withstand "
"attacks both from quantum and classical computing systems. This is also "
"sometimes called **quantum-resistant**, or **post-quantum cryptography**.`\n"
msgstr ""
"Bidang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Juga dikenal sebagai Post Quantum "
"atau Quantum-Resistant. Algoritma kriptografi, protokol, atau sistem yang "
"dirancang untuk menahan serangan dari komputer kuantum. Seiring kemajuan "
"teknologi komputasi kuantum, keamanan komunikasi digital dan informasi "
"sensitif perlu tetap terjaga.\">**kriptografi quantum-"
"safe**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) mencakup upaya untuk [mengidentifikasi dan "
"mengembangkan skema kriptografi](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) "
"yang dapat menahan serangan baik dari sistem komputasi kuantum maupun "
"klasikal. Ini kadang juga disebut **quantum-resistant**, atau **kriptografi "
"post-kuantum**.`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In earlier lessons, we discussed some of the potential security risks that "
"the development of general-purpose quantum computers poses to a number of "
"traditional cryptographic primitives such as symmetric key algorithms, "
"cryptographic hash functions, and asymmetric key algorithms. Additionally, "
"we mentioned cryptographically relevant quantum algorithms and the protocols"
" they impact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran-pelajaran sebelumnya, kita membahas beberapa potensi risiko "
"keamanan yang ditimbulkan oleh pengembangan komputer kuantum tujuan umum "
"terhadap sejumlah primitif kriptografi tradisional seperti algoritma kunci "
"simetris, fungsi hash kriptografi, dan algoritma kunci asimetris. Selain "
"itu, kita menyebutkan algoritma kuantum yang relevan secara kriptografis dan"
" protokol yang mereka pengaruhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that the most significant impacts of quantum algorithms occur in the "
"context of asymmetric key cryptography, where [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) offers a polynomial-"
"time solution to the prime factoring and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Discrete Logarithm Problem. Finding the exponent to which a "
"given number (the base) must be raised to obtain another number (the "
"result), within a specified mathematical group. Solving this problem for "
"certain groups is computationally difficult, forming the basis for several "
"cryptographic schemes but Quantum Computers may have the potential to solve "
"this problem in the future.\">discrete logarithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"problems. Therefore, asymmetric cryptosystems based on factoring and "
"discrete logarithms need to be replaced by new quantum-safe cryptography "
"schemes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahwa dampak paling signifikan dari algoritma kuantum terjadi "
"dalam konteks kriptografi kunci asimetris, di mana [algoritma "
"Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) menawarkan solusi waktu "
"polinomial untuk masalah faktorisasi prima dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Masalah Logaritma Diskret. Menemukan eksponen yang harus "
"dipangkatkan pada bilangan tertentu (basis) untuk mendapatkan bilangan lain "
"(hasil), dalam grup matematis yang ditentukan. Memecahkan masalah ini untuk "
"grup tertentu secara komputasional sulit, membentuk dasar untuk beberapa "
"skema kriptografi tetapi Komputer Kuantum mungkin memiliki potensi untuk "
"memecahkan masalah ini di masa depan.\">logaritma "
"diskret</DefinitionTooltip>. Oleh karena itu, sistem kriptografi asimetris "
"berbasis faktorisasi dan logaritma diskret perlu diganti dengan skema "
"kriptografi quantum-safe yang baru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is in contrast to the symmetric key and cryptographic hashing protocols"
" impacted by the Grover and [BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319) "
"algorithms, where the quantum speedups are not super-polynomial. Therefore, "
"in this latter case, existing algorithms such as AES and SHA-256 can be "
"fortified at least in the medium term by ensuring sufficiently long key and "
"hash lengths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini berbeda dengan protokol kunci simetris dan hashing kriptografi yang "
"terpengaruh oleh algoritma Grover dan "
"[BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319), di mana percepatan kuantum tidak "
"bersifat super-polinomial. Oleh karena itu, dalam kasus yang terakhir, "
"algoritma yang ada seperti AES dan SHA-256 dapat diperkuat setidaknya dalam "
"jangka menengah dengan memastikan panjang kunci dan hash yang cukup.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms and impacts to cryptography {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum dan dampaknya pada kriptografi {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum Algorithm | Functionality      | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"As defined by the [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *A number characterizing the amount of work that is expected to suffice to defeat an implemented cryptographic mechanism (for example, by compromising its functionality and/or circumventing the protection that its use was intended to facilitate). Security strength is often expressed in bits. If the security strength of a particular implementation of a cryptographic mechanism is s bits, it is expected that the equivalent of (roughly) 2<sup>s</sup> basic operations of some sort will be sufficient to defeat it in some way.*\">Security Strength</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = number of bits) | Impacted Cryptographic Protocols                 | Mitigation             |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | factoring          | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | discrete logarithm | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Elliptic Curve Cryptography | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | key search         | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Symmetric key algorithms (for example, AES)             | Sufficient key length  |\n"
"| Grover            | pre-image attack   | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
"| BHT               | collision attack   | $2^{n/3}$ or $2^{2n/5}$                              | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Algoritma Kuantum | Fungsionalitas      | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Sebagaimana didefinisikan oleh [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *Angka yang mencirikan jumlah pekerjaan yang diharapkan cukup untuk mengalahkan mekanisme kriptografi yang diimplementasikan (misalnya, dengan mengkompromikan fungsionalitasnya dan/atau menghindari perlindungan yang dimaksudkan penggunaannya untuk memfasilitasi). Kekuatan keamanan sering dinyatakan dalam bit. Jika kekuatan keamanan dari implementasi mekanisme kriptografi tertentu adalah s bit, diharapkan setara dengan (kira-kira) 2<sup>s</sup> operasi dasar semacam itu akan cukup untuk mengalahkannya dengan cara tertentu.*\">Kekuatan Keamanan</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = jumlah bit) | Protokol Kriptografi yang Terpengaruh                 | Mitigasi             |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | faktorisasi          | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Migrasi ke QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | logaritma diskret | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Elliptic Curve Cryptography | Migrasi ke QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | pencarian kunci         | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Algoritma kunci simetris (misalnya, AES)             | Panjang kunci yang cukup  |\n"
"| Grover            | serangan pre-image   | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Fungsi hash (misalnya, SHA-256)                   | Panjang hash yang cukup |\n"
"| BHT               | serangan tabrakan   | $2^{n/3}$ or $2^{2n/5}$                              | Fungsi hash (misalnya, SHA-256)                   | Panjang hash yang cukup |\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic principles of quantum-safe cryptography {#basic-principles-of-quantum-"
"safe-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Prinsip dasar kriptografi quantum-safe {#basic-principles-of-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Computational complexity {#computational-complexity}"
msgstr "Kompleksitas komputasional {#computational-complexity}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In cryptography, the *computational complexity class* [**NP (non-"
"deterministic polynomial "
"time)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" plays an important role. This class consists of decision problems for which"
" proposed solutions can be verified in polynomial time using a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Machine that operates on an infinite tape "
"containing symbols which has a read/write head that can move left or right "
"on the tape and change the symbols according to a set of predetermined "
"rules. In a deterministic Turing machine, the transition from one state to "
"another is uniquely determined by the current state and the symbol being "
"read from the tape. This means that for any given configuration of the "
"machine, there is only one possible next step.\">deterministic Turing "
"machine</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). The importance of NP stems from the fact "
"that it is conjectured to consist of many computational problems that cannot"
" be solved efficiently by both classical and quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kriptografi, *kelas kompleksitas komputasional* [**NP (non-"
"deterministic polynomial "
"time)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" memainkan peran penting. Kelas ini terdiri dari masalah keputusan yang "
"solusi yang diusulkan dapat diverifikasi dalam waktu polinomial menggunakan "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mesin yang beroperasi pada pita tak terbatas"
" yang berisi simbol yang memiliki kepala baca/tulis yang dapat bergerak ke "
"kiri atau kanan pada pita dan mengubah simbol sesuai seperangkat aturan yang"
" telah ditentukan. Dalam mesin Turing deterministik, transisi dari satu "
"state ke state lainnya ditentukan secara unik oleh state saat ini dan simbol"
" yang sedang dibaca dari pita. Ini berarti bahwa untuk konfigurasi mesin "
"tertentu, hanya ada satu langkah berikutnya yang mungkin.\">mesin Turing "
"deterministik</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). Pentingnya NP berasal dari fakta "
"bahwa ia diperkirakan terdiri dari banyak masalah komputasional yang tidak "
"dapat diselesaikan secara efisien oleh komputer klasikal maupun kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first generation of successful asymmetric key cryptosystems developed in"
" the 1970s based their security on mathematical problems such as prime "
"factorization and discrete logarithms that are now conjectured to belong to "
"the **NP-intermediate** subclass of NP. This subclass consists of problems "
"that are believed not to have polynomial-time solutions on DTMs but at the "
"same time are also not as hard as the hardest problems in NP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Generasi pertama sistem kriptografi kunci asimetris yang berhasil "
"dikembangkan pada tahun 1970-an mendasarkan keamanannya pada masalah "
"matematika seperti faktorisasi prima dan logaritma diskret yang sekarang "
"diperkirakan termasuk dalam subkelas **NP-intermediate** dari NP. Subkelas "
"ini terdiri dari masalah yang diyakini tidak memiliki solusi waktu "
"polinomial pada DTM tetapi pada saat yang sama juga tidak sesulit masalah "
"tersulit dalam NP.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The latter belong to the subclass [**NP-"
"complete**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Following [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) in the 1990s, it became"
" clear that at least some NP-intermediate problems are amenable to efficient"
" solutions on quantum computers that are not DTMs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang terakhir termasuk dalam subkelas [**NP-"
"complete**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Mengikuti [algoritma "
"Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) pada tahun 1990-an, menjadi "
"jelas bahwa setidaknya beberapa masalah NP-intermediate dapat diselesaikan "
"secara efisien di komputer kuantum yang bukan DTM.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, modern quantum-safe cryptography schemes are based on NP-complete"
" problems or related [**NP-"
"hard**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) problems, which currently are not known to be "
"solvable efficiently even on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, skema kriptografi quantum-safe modern didasarkan pada "
"masalah NP-complete atau masalah [**NP-"
"hard**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) terkait, yang saat ini tidak diketahui dapat "
"diselesaikan secara efisien bahkan di komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Average vs worst-case hardness {#average-vs-worst-case-hardness}"
msgstr ""
"Kesulitan kasus rata-rata vs kasus terburuk {#average-vs-worst-case-"
"hardness}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While there are many known NP-hard problems, not every such problem is "
"suitable as a basis for cryptographic security. In this context, the notion "
"of [**average-case "
"hardness**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" is useful for cryptography. A problem is **average-case hard** if most "
"instances of the problem drawn randomly from some distribution are hard, "
"whereas a problem is **worst-case hard** if it is hard only on some isolated"
" *worst-case* instances. Quantum-safe cryptologists therefore search for "
"mathematical problems that satisfy the assumption of average-case hardness "
"and employ theoretical tools such as worst-case to average-case "
"[reductions](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) to identify suitable protocols"
" whose security and efficiency can be guaranteed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun ada banyak masalah NP-hard yang diketahui, tidak setiap masalah "
"seperti itu cocok sebagai dasar untuk keamanan kriptografi. Dalam konteks "
"ini, gagasan [**kesulitan kasus rata-"
"rata**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" berguna untuk kriptografi. Suatu masalah bersifat **hard kasus rata-rata** "
"jika sebagian besar instance masalah yang diambil secara acak dari beberapa "
"distribusi bersifat hard, sedangkan masalah bersifat **hard kasus terburuk**"
" jika hanya sulit pada beberapa instance *kasus terburuk* yang terisolasi. "
"Kriptologis quantum-safe oleh karena itu mencari masalah matematika yang "
"memenuhi asumsi kesulitan kasus rata-rata dan menggunakan alat teoritis "
"seperti reduksi kasus terburuk ke kasus rata-rata "
"[reductions](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) untuk mengidentifikasi "
"protokol yang cocok yang keamanan dan efisiensinya dapat dijamin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical structures {#mathematical-structures}"
msgstr "Struktur matematika {#mathematical-structures}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptologists have put forth a number of different mathematical structures "
"that satisfy the necessary hardness requirements as potential candidates for"
" quantum-safe migration of asymmetric key cryptosystems. Some well-known "
"families include:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para kriptologis telah mengusulkan sejumlah struktur matematika berbeda yang"
" memenuhi persyaratan kekerasan yang diperlukan sebagai kandidat potensial "
"untuk migrasi quantum-safe dari sistem kriptografi kunci asimetris. Beberapa"
" keluarga yang terkenal meliputi:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Lattice-based cryptography:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) This "
"class of algorithms relies on the hardness of problems such as the shortest "
"vector problem (SVP) and the closest vector problem (CVP) in [lattice "
"structures](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Notable lattice-based schemes include "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) and"
" [Learning with Errors](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berbasis lattice:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) Kelas "
"algoritma ini mengandalkan kesulitan masalah seperti shortest vector problem"
" (SVP) dan closest vector problem (CVP) dalam [struktur "
"lattice](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Skema berbasis lattice yang terkenal termasuk "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) dan"
" [Learning with Errors](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Code-based cryptography:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) "
"This type of cryptography is based on the difficulty of decoding a general "
"linear code. The most notable example is the [McEliece "
"cryptosystem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berbasis "
"kode:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) Jenis kriptografi ini "
"didasarkan pada kesulitan mendekode kode linier umum. Contoh paling terkenal"
" adalah [sistem kriptografi "
"McEliece](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Multivariate "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" These systems involve equations of multiple variables over a finite field. "
"A well-known system in this category is the HFE (Hidden Field Equations) "
"scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi "
"multivariat:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" Sistem ini melibatkan persamaan berbagai variabel atas bidang hingga. "
"Sistem yang terkenal dalam kategori ini adalah skema HFE (Hidden Field "
"Equations).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Hash-based "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) These are cryptographic systems that "
"use only cryptographic hash functions. They are often used for digital "
"signatures, like the Merkle signature scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berbasis "
"hash:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) Ini adalah sistem kriptografi yang "
"hanya menggunakan fungsi hash kriptografi. Mereka sering digunakan untuk "
"tanda tangan digital, seperti skema tanda tangan Merkle.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Isogeny-based "
"cryptography:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" These systems are based on the difficulty of certain problems in the "
"algebraic structure of elliptic curves. [Supersingular Isogeny Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) is an example.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berbasis "
"isogeny:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" Sistem ini didasarkan pada kesulitan masalah tertentu dalam struktur "
"aljabar kurva eliptik. [Supersingular Isogeny Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) adalah contohnya.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NIST standardization of quantum-safe cryptography {#nist-standardization-of-"
"quantum-safe-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Standardisasi NIST tentang kriptografi quantum-safe {#nist-standardization-"
"of-quantum-safe-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recognizing the potential impact of quantum computing on current "
"cryptographic systems, NIST initiated a program to standardize quantum-safe "
"cryptographic algorithms in 2016 using a process similar to the one NIST "
"followed to standardize the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) in the early "
"2000s. In an open and transparent process involving security domain "
"stakeholders, several QSC candidates were submitted for evaluation, and "
"following a six-year review process, [NIST announced a list of four "
"finalists](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-"
"first-four-quantum-resistant-cryptographic-algorithms) to become a part of "
"NIST’s quantum-safe cryptographic standard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menyadari potensi dampak komputasi kuantum pada sistem kriptografi saat ini,"
" NIST memulai program untuk menstandarisasi algoritma kriptografi quantum-"
"safe pada tahun 2016 menggunakan proses yang mirip dengan yang diikuti NIST "
"untuk menstandarisasi Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) pada awal tahun "
"2000-an. Dalam proses yang terbuka dan transparan yang melibatkan pemangku "
"kepentingan domain keamanan, beberapa kandidat QSC diajukan untuk evaluasi, "
"dan setelah proses tinjauan enam tahun, [NIST mengumumkan daftar empat "
"finalis](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-first-"
"four-quantum-resistant-cryptographic-algorithms) untuk menjadi bagian dari "
"standar kriptografi quantum-safe NIST.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finalists of the first NIST quantum-safe cryptography standardization effort"
" {#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-standardization-"
"effort}"
msgstr ""
"Finalis dari upaya standardisasi kriptografi quantum-safe NIST pertama "
"{#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-standardization-"
"effort}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| QSC Algorithm      | Cryptographic family | Application                     |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Lattice-based        | Key encapsulation mechanism     |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Lattice-based        | Digital signatures              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Lattice-based        | Lightweight digital signatures |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Hash-based           | Digital Signatures              |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Algoritma QSC      | Keluarga kriptografi | Aplikasi                     |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Berbasis lattice        | Mekanisme enkapsulasi kunci     |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Berbasis lattice        | Tanda tangan digital              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Berbasis lattice        | Tanda tangan digital ringan |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Berbasis hash           | Tanda tangan digital              |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of the four NIST finalists, three are lattice-based and one, "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), is hash-based. The Kyber and Dilithium "
"algorithms, part of the [CRYSTALS cryptographic suite](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/), were selected to be general-purpose protocols for key "
"encapsulation and digital signatures, respectively. "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" was recommended for applications requiring smaller digital signatures than "
"those provided by Dilithium. [SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) meanwhile was "
"primarily chosen as a backup option to the lattice-based approaches, as it "
"uses a different mathematical structure. Lattice-based cryptography "
"therefore seems well-positioned to form the basis for the first-generation "
"of QSC standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari empat finalis NIST, tiga berbasis lattice dan satu, "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), berbasis hash. Algoritma Kyber dan "
"Dilithium, bagian dari [suite kriptografi CRYSTALS](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/), dipilih sebagai protokol tujuan umum untuk enkapsulasi kunci"
" dan tanda tangan digital, masing-masing. "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" direkomendasikan untuk aplikasi yang memerlukan tanda tangan digital yang "
"lebih kecil dari yang disediakan oleh Dilithium. "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) sementara itu terutama dipilih sebagai opsi"
" cadangan untuk pendekatan berbasis lattice, karena menggunakan struktur "
"matematika yang berbeda. Kriptografi berbasis lattice oleh karena itu "
"tampaknya berada dalam posisi yang baik untuk membentuk dasar generasi "
"pertama standar QSC.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In August 2023, [NIST published three draft standards](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) for comments - which include the algorithms above:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada Agustus 2023, [NIST menerbitkan tiga draf standar](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) untuk komentar - yang mencakup algoritma di atas:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattice-based cryptography {#lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi berbasis lattice {#lattice-based-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the name suggests, [lattice-based "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) is based on the hardness of "
"certain problems defined on mathematical structures called "
"[**lattices**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti namanya, [kriptografi berbasis "
"lattice](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) didasarkan pada kesulitan masalah"
" tertentu yang didefinisikan pada struktur matematika yang disebut "
"[**lattice**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of fundamental importance are two computational problems on lattices, namely"
" the **shortest vector problem** and the **learning with errors problem**, "
"which we discuss below after some preliminary definitions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang sangat penting adalah dua masalah komputasional pada lattice, yaitu "
"**shortest vector problem** dan **learning with errors problem**, yang kita "
"bahas di bawah setelah beberapa definisi awal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattices {#lattices}"
msgstr "Lattice {#lattices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think of what a lattice is in the world around us. The Eiffel tower "
"(Paris), or Birds-nest stadium (Beijing). Those structures have many linked "
"elements which can be thought of as a series of points joined together along"
" straight lines.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa membayangkan apa itu lattice di dunia sekitar kita. Menara Eiffel "
"(Paris), atau stadion Birds-nest (Beijing). Struktur-struktur itu memiliki "
"banyak elemen yang terhubung yang dapat dianggap sebagai serangkaian titik "
"yang dihubungkan bersama sepanjang garis lurus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diamonds are another form of lattice. There is a clear, repeating structure "
"of Carbon atoms. They are then effectively joined together by atomic bonds; "
"and this structure that is formed is what gives diamond its unique "
"properties. However, different crystal structures can have very different "
"layouts (can be thought of as our lattice structure), and therefore ends up "
"with distinct features. Hence, lattices serve as the foundational "
"mathematical framework that dictates the unique traits of different "
"structures which we use in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berlian adalah bentuk lattice lainnya. Ada struktur atom Karbon yang jelas "
"dan berulang. Mereka kemudian secara efektif dihubungkan oleh ikatan atom; "
"dan struktur yang terbentuk inilah yang memberikan berlian sifat-sifat "
"uniknya. Namun, struktur kristal yang berbeda dapat memiliki tata letak yang"
" sangat berbeda (dapat dianggap sebagai struktur lattice kita), dan oleh "
"karena itu menghasilkan fitur yang berbeda. Oleh karena itu, lattice "
"berfungsi sebagai kerangka matematis dasar yang menentukan sifat unik dari "
"struktur yang berbeda yang kita gunakan dalam kriptografi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simple mathematical terms, a lattice can be thought of as a collection of"
" regularly spaced points that repeat at fixed intervals. To describe how "
"these points are positioned relative to each other, we use vectors. The "
"specific arrangement of these vectors, which defines the layout of the "
"lattice, is referred to as the *basis.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam istilah matematis sederhana, lattice dapat dianggap sebagai kumpulan "
"titik-titik yang berjarak teratur yang berulang pada interval tetap. Untuk "
"menggambarkan bagaimana titik-titik ini diposisikan relatif satu sama lain, "
"kita menggunakan vektor. Susunan spesifik vektor-vektor ini, yang "
"mendefinisikan tata letak lattice, disebut sebagai *basis.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine you have a box of toy construction bricks, and you want to build "
"various objects with the same set of pieces. Each unique object you create "
"requires a specific arrangement, and the way you choose and arrange the "
"bricks serves as the *basis* for constructing different objects. If you "
"change the selection or arrangement of bricks, you get a different object "
"with distinct characteristics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bayangkan kamu punya kotak batu bata konstruksi mainan, dan kamu ingin "
"membangun berbagai objek dengan set potongan yang sama. Setiap objek unik "
"yang kamu buat memerlukan susunan tertentu, dan cara kamu memilih dan "
"menyusun batu bata berfungsi sebagai *basis* untuk membangun objek yang "
"berbeda. Jika kamu mengubah pilihan atau susunan batu bata, kamu mendapatkan"
" objek yang berbeda dengan karakteristik yang berbeda.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, in a lattice, the *basis* is like the set of atomic building "
"blocks that define the lattice's structure. Depending on how you arrange "
"these building blocks (atoms or points) in the lattice, you can create "
"various lattice structures with different properties. Just as changing the "
"toy construction brick pieces changes the object you build, altering the "
"basis changes the lattice's characteristics and properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"Demikian pula, dalam lattice, *basis* seperti seperangkat blok bangunan atom"
" yang mendefinisikan struktur lattice. Tergantung bagaimana kamu menyusun "
"blok-blok bangunan ini (atom atau titik) dalam lattice, kamu bisa membuat "
"berbagai struktur lattice dengan sifat yang berbeda. Sama seperti mengubah "
"potongan batu bata konstruksi mainan mengubah objek yang kamu bangun, "
"mengubah basis mengubah karakteristik dan sifat lattice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's important to note that lattices are not limited to two or three "
"dimensions; they can extend to higher dimensions, and in fields like "
"cryptography, they may involve 1000s or more dimensions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk dicatat bahwa lattice tidak terbatas pada dua atau tiga "
"dimensi; mereka bisa meluas ke dimensi yang lebih tinggi, dan dalam bidang "
"seperti kriptografi, mereka mungkin melibatkan 1000-an dimensi atau lebih.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of lattices\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Deskripsi matematis dari lattice\">\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given $n$ linearly independent vectors $A = "
"\\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | \\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, "
"the *lattice* $\\mathcal{L}$ generated by $A$ is the set of integer linear "
"combinations $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i \\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan $n$ vektor yang linearly independent $A = "
"\\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | \\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, "
"*lattice* $\\mathcal{L}$ yang dihasilkan oleh $A$ adalah himpunan kombinasi "
"linier integer $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i \\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A *basis* $B$ of a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ is any set of linearly independent"
" vectors $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$  that spans the lattice i.e, $\\mathcal{L}(B)"
" = \\{ \\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebuah *basis* $B$ dari lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ adalah himpunan vektor "
"linearly independent $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$  yang membentangkan lattice "
"yaitu, $\\mathcal{L}(B) = \\{ \\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Importantly, the basis for a given lattice is not unique. Two different "
"basis sets $B, B^{\\prime}$ can describe the same lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang penting, basis untuk lattice tertentu tidak unik. Dua set basis yang "
"berbeda $B, B^{\\prime}$ dapat menggambarkan lattice yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every basis is unique - it may just be a different perspective of the "
"same structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak setiap basis unik - itu mungkin hanya perspektif yang berbeda dari "
"struktur yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This leads to an important concept in lattice mathematics, that of "
"[*lattice-basis "
"reduction*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" This is the process of taking a given integer lattice and attempting to "
"find a *good* basis comprising short, nearly orthogonal vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini mengarah pada konsep penting dalam matematika lattice, yaitu "
"[*pengurangan basis "
"lattice*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" Ini adalah proses mengambil lattice integer tertentu dan mencoba menemukan "
"basis *baik* yang terdiri dari vektor-vektor pendek, hampir ortogonal.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis v_1,"
" v_2 to a good basis u_1, u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 1: Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis v_1,"
" v_2 to a good basis u_1, u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis "
"$v_1$, $v_2$ to a good basis $u_1$, $u_2$*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 1. Pengurangan basis lattice dalam dua dimensi dari basis \"buruk\" "
"$v_1$, $v_2$ ke basis baik $u_1$, $u_2$*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lattice-basis reductions can be performed in polynomial-time using the "
"[**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász** "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengurangan basis lattice dapat dilakukan dalam waktu polinomial menggunakan"
" algoritma "
"[**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The shortest vector problem {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Shortest vector problem {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **shortest vector problem** (SVP) is the challenge of finding the "
"shortest distance (vector), between any two points in the lattice\n"
msgstr ""
"**Shortest vector problem** (SVP) adalah tantangan menemukan jarak (vektor) "
"terpendek antara dua titik mana pun dalam lattice\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the SVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Deskripsi matematis dari SVP\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ "
"with norm $N$, the "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" asks for the shortest non-zero vector in $\\mathcal{L}$ as measured by $N$,"
" that is, find a vector $v$ such that its length $\\|v\\|_N = "
"\\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ yang tertanam dalam ruang vektor "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ dengan norm $N$, "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" meminta vektor bukan-nol terpendek dalam $\\mathcal{L}$ yang diukur oleh "
"$N$, yaitu temukan vektor $v$ sehingga panjangnya $\\|v\\|_N = "
"\\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 2: The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The "
"orange vector is the shortest vector](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 2: The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The "
"orange vector is the shortest vector](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" yellow vector is the shortest vector*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 2. SVP pada lattice yang ditentukan oleh vektor basis $b_1$, $b_2$: "
"Vektor kuning adalah vektor terpendek*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Miklós Ajtai has shown that the shortest vector problem is **NP-"
"hard**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) in the worst case for "
"certain random lattices, even when lattice-basis reduction to a *good* basis"
" is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Miklós Ajtai telah menunjukkan bahwa shortest vector problem bersifat **NP-"
"hard**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) dalam kasus terburuk "
"untuk lattice acak tertentu, bahkan ketika pengurangan basis lattice ke "
"basis *baik* memungkinkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ajtai also demonstrated that there exists a worst-case to average-case "
"reduction for the shortest vector problem, laying the foundation for its use"
" in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ajtai juga mendemonstrasikan bahwa ada reduksi kasus terburuk ke kasus rata-"
"rata untuk shortest vector problem, meletakkan dasar untuk penggunaannya "
"dalam kriptografi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The closest vector problem {#the-closest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Closest vector problem {#the-closest-vector-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the **closest vector problem** (CVP) we are looking to find the closest "
"point on the lattice to the origin, or location given.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam **closest vector problem** (CVP) kita mencari titik terdekat pada "
"lattice ke titik asal, atau lokasi yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CVP is also known to be NP-hard.\n"
msgstr "CVP juga diketahui bersifat NP-hard.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 3: The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The red "
"point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external vector "
"shown in green that is not on the lattice](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 3: The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The red "
"point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external vector "
"shown in green that is not on the lattice](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 3. The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" red point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external "
"vector shown in green that is not on the lattice*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Gambar 3. CVP pada lattice yang ditentukan oleh vektor basis $b_1$, $b_2$: "
"Titik merah mewakili vektor lattice terdekat ke vektor eksternal yang "
"diberikan yang ditunjukkan dalam hijau yang tidak berada di lattice*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *shortest vector problem* is a special case of the *closest vector "
"problem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Shortest vector problem* adalah kasus khusus dari *closest vector "
"problem*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of CVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Deskripsi matematis dari CVP\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ with "
"metric $M$ is given, along with a vector $v$ in $\\mathcal{V}$ but not "
"necessarily in $\\mathcal{L}$. The task then is to find the vector $u$ in "
"$\\mathcal{L}$ closest to $v$ as measured by $M$ that is, $d_M (u, v) = "
"\\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ where "
"$d_M$ is the distance function of the metric $M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ yang tertanam dalam ruang vektor "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ dengan metrik $M$, bersama dengan vektor $v$ dalam "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ tetapi tidak harus dalam $\\mathcal{L}$. Tugasnya kemudian "
"adalah menemukan vektor $u$ dalam $\\mathcal{L}$ yang paling dekat ke $v$ "
"yang diukur oleh $M$ yaitu, $d_M (u, v) = \\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in "
"\\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ di mana $d_M$ adalah fungsi jarak dari "
"metrik $M$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bounded distance decoding problem {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-"
"problem}"
msgstr ""
"Bounded distance decoding problem {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Very similar to the CVP is the [**bounded distance "
"decoding**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD) problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sangat mirip dengan CVP adalah masalah [**bounded distance "
"decoding**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case we know that the origin supplied is close to the lattice, but "
"not *how close*, ie *bounded*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam hal ini kita tahu bahwa titik asal yang diberikan dekat dengan "
"lattice, tetapi tidak *seberapa dekat*, yaitu *bounded*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the BDD problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Deskripsi matematis dari masalah BDD\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is additionally specified that the external vector $v$ is at most within "
"a distance $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, where $\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ "
"is the length of the shortest vector in the lattice and $\\sigma$ is a small"
" parameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu ditentukan bahwa vektor eksternal $v$ berada paling jauh dalam "
"jarak $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, di mana $\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ "
"adalah panjang vektor terpendek dalam lattice dan $\\sigma$ adalah parameter"
" kecil.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The learning with errors problem {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"
msgstr "Learning with errors problem {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem is based on the mathematics of "
"lattices combined with the idea of introducing errors into an equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah learning with errors (LWE) didasarkan pada matematika lattice yang "
"dikombinasikan dengan ide memasukkan kesalahan ke dalam persamaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As is the case with any mathematical basis for cryptographic algorithms we "
"can easily introduce noise as we make a series of calculations, but trying "
"to find the inverse is very difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti halnya basis matematis untuk algoritma kriptografi apa pun, kita "
"bisa dengan mudah memasukkan noise saat kita melakukan serangkaian "
"perhitungan, tetapi mencoba menemukan inversnya sangat sulit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of the LWE problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika masalah LWE\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [learning with errors "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ with modulus $q$ and error distribution $\\chi$"
" is: Given access only to polynomially many samples $(\\mathbf {a} ,t)$ of "
"choice from Alice's distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"learn\" and "
"output the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah [learning with "
"errors](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ dengan modulus $q$ dan distribusi kesalahan "
"$\\chi$ adalah: Diberikan akses hanya ke sampel polinomial $(\\mathbf {a} "
",t)$ pilihan dari distribusi Alice $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"pelajari\" "
"dan keluarkan vektor rahasia ${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ be the ring of integers modulo $q$.\n"
msgstr "Misalkan ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ adalah ring integer modulo $q$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ be the set of $n$-dimensional vectors over "
"${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ adalah himpunan vektor $n$-dimensi atas "
"${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An adversary — say, Alice — chooses a fixed vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and keeps it a secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seorang adversary — katakanlah, Alice — memilih vektor tetap ${\\mathbf{s}} "
"\\in {\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ dan menyimpannya sebagai rahasia.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice also specifies $\\chi$, a fixed \"error\" probability distribution "
"over $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice juga menentukan $\\chi$, distribusi probabilitas \"kesalahan\" tetap "
"atas $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the above ingredients, she constructs a distribution "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ on ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} "
"_{q}}$ as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan bahan-bahan di atas, dia membangun distribusi "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ pada ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} "
"_{q}}$ sebagai berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the uniform distribution over ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, Alice chooses a "
"vector ${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari distribusi seragam atas ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, Alice memilih vektor "
"${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the given distribution $\\chi$, she picks a number $ {\\displaystyle "
"\\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dari distribusi yang diberikan $\\chi$, dia memilih bilangan $ "
"{\\displaystyle \\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She then evaluates ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} ,\\mathbf {s} "
"\\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, where $\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle "
"=\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ is the standard inner product on "
"${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and the addition is in $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dia kemudian mengevaluasi ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} ,\\mathbf "
"{s} \\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, di mana "
"$\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle =\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ adalah hasil "
"kali dalam standar pada ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ dan penambahan dalam "
"$\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice outputs ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"
msgstr "Alice mengeluarkan ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Note the errors introduced: $\\varepsilon$ drawn from $\\chi$\n"
msgstr ""
"    Catat kesalahan yang diperkenalkan: $\\varepsilon$ ditarik dari "
"$\\chi$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Early developments in the LWE problem employed the one-dimensional "
"discrete Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ as the error "
"distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Perkembangan awal dalam masalah LWE menggunakan distribusi Gaussian "
"diskret satu dimensi pada $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ sebagai distribusi "
"kesalahan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remarkable feature of the LWE problem is that without the errors, it "
"reduces to a set of linear equations that can be easily solved using a "
"technique like Gaussian elimination.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fitur luar biasa dari masalah LWE adalah bahwa tanpa kesalahan, masalah ini "
"tereduksi menjadi serangkaian persamaan linier yang dapat diselesaikan "
"dengan mudah menggunakan teknik seperti eliminasi Gaussian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the inclusion of a suitable error distribution renders it an NP-"
"hard problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Namun, penyertaan distribusi kesalahan yang sesuai membuatnya menjadi "
"masalah NP-hard.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption using the Learning with Errors cryptosystem {#encryption-using-"
"the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"
msgstr ""
"Enkripsi menggunakan sistem kriptografi Learning with Errors {#encryption-"
"using-the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LWE problem discussed above leads to a public key cryptosystem "
"introduced by [Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah LWE yang dibahas di atas mengarah ke sistem kriptografi kunci publik"
" yang diperkenalkan oleh [Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The exact process will be covered in the Python example below.\n"
msgstr "Proses pastinya akan dibahas dalam contoh Python di bawah ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of key generation, encryption, and decryption\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika pembuatan kunci, enkripsi, dan dekripsi\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameters:** The cryptosystem is characterized by the vector dimension or"
" security parameter $n$, modulus $q$, number of LWE samples $N$, and error "
"distribution $\\chi$. Typical choices that guarantee both security and "
"correctness are:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parameter:** Sistem kriptografi dicirikan oleh dimensi vektor atau "
"parameter keamanan $n$, modulus $q$, jumlah sampel LWE $N$, dan distribusi "
"kesalahan $\\chi$. Pilihan tipikal yang menjamin keamanan dan kebenaran "
"adalah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a prime between $n^2$ and $2n^2$\n"
msgstr "$q$ adalah bilangan prima antara $n^2$ dan $2n^2$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"
msgstr "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, with $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, where "
"$\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ is obtained by sampling the normal distribution "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ and reducing the result modulo 1\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, dengan $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, di "
"mana $\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ diperoleh dengan mengambil sampel distribusi normal "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ dan mereduksi hasilnya modulo 1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key:** The private key is the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kunci privat:** Kunci privat adalah vektor rahasia ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key:** Choose $N$ samples $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ from the "
"LWE distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kunci publik:** Pilih $N$ sampel $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ dari "
"distribusi LWE $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Enkripsi:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encryption utilizes the public key and is carried out bit by bit.\n"
msgstr "Enkripsi memanfaatkan kunci publik dan dilakukan bit per bit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each bit of the message, randomly choose a binary vector $\\mathbf{r} "
"\\in \\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk setiap bit pesan, pilih secara acak vektor biner $\\mathbf{r} \\in "
"\\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 0, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bit pesan adalah 0, enkripsinya adalah $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 1, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bit pesan adalah 1, enkripsinya adalah $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Decryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Dekripsi:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The decryption utilizes the private key ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"
msgstr "Dekripsi memanfaatkan kunci privat ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pair $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ decrypts to $0$ if $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ is closer to $0$ than "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, else it decrypts to 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasangan $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ mendekripsi ke $0$ jika $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ lebih dekat ke $0$ daripada "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, jika tidak maka mendekripsi ke "
"1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The security of the LWE public key cryptosystem was analyzed by Regev:\n"
msgstr "Keamanan sistem kriptografi kunci publik LWE dianalisis oleh Regev:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Firstly, it was shown that recovering the error/noise vector $\\mathbf{e} = "
"[\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ involved in the "
"construction of the public key is as hard as the bounded distance decoding "
"(BDD) problem, which, as noted above, is believed to be NP-hard. This "
"establishes the correspondence between LWE and explicit lattice problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, ditunjukkan bahwa memulihkan vektor kesalahan/noise $\\mathbf{e} = "
"[\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ yang terlibat dalam"
" konstruksi kunci publik sama sulitnya dengan masalah bounded distance "
"decoding (BDD), yang, seperti disebutkan di atas, diyakini NP-hard. Ini "
"membangun korespondensi antara LWE dan masalah lattice eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Secondly, security against chosen plain text attacks (CPA) is based on the "
"observation that an algorithm for distinguishing between encryptions of 0 "
"and 1 in the above cryptosystem can also distinguish between the "
"distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ and the uniform distribution over "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, which would imply a solution "
"of LWE itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua, keamanan terhadap serangan chosen plain text (CPA) didasarkan pada "
"pengamatan bahwa algoritma untuk membedakan antara enkripsi 0 dan 1 dalam "
"sistem kriptografi di atas juga dapat membedakan antara distribusi "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ dan distribusi seragam atas $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} "
"\\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, yang akan mengimplikasikan solusi dari LWE itu "
"sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of LWE encryption in Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-"
"in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Ilustrasi enkripsi LWE dalam Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-in-"
"python}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following simple example shows the use of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Learning With Errors. A mathematical technique which hides "
"secret information by introducing errors into equations, making them harder "
"to solve.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> for encryption and decryption. Bob will "
"send an encrypted message to Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh sederhana berikut menunjukkan penggunaan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Learning With Errors. Teknik matematis yang menyembunyikan "
"informasi rahasia dengan memasukkan kesalahan ke dalam persamaan, membuatnya"
" lebih sulit dipecahkan.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> untuk enkripsi dan "
"dekripsi. Bob akan mengirim pesan terenkripsi ke Alice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on the **problem parameters**. These are "
"explained in detail in the maths section above, but in summary we require "
"$n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob menyepakati **parameter masalah**. Ini dijelaskan "
"secara rinci di bagian matematika di atas, tetapi secara ringkas kita "
"memerlukan $n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start with some of the basic parameters\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan beberapa parameter dasar\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N$ represents the number of samples\n"
msgstr "$N$ mewakili jumlah sampel\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a modulus\n"
msgstr "$q$ adalah modulus\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "n is known as the security parameter, or vector dimension.\n"
msgstr "n dikenal sebagai parameter keamanan, atau dimensi vektor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These parameters are all public information in principle.\n"
msgstr ""
"Parameter-parameter ini semuanya merupakan informasi publik pada "
"prinsipnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We also need a way of introducing errors\n"
msgstr "Kita juga membutuhkan cara untuk memasukkan kesalahan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\chi$ represent the errors we want to introduce - we use a discrete "
"Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ characterized by mean 0 and "
"standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $\\chi$ mewakili kesalahan yang ingin kita masukkan - kita "
"menggunakan distribusi Gaussian diskret pada $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ yang "
"dicirikan oleh rata-rata 0 dan standar deviasi $\\sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This definition of the errors to introduce is also public.\n"
msgstr "Definisi kesalahan yang akan dimasukkan ini juga bersifat publik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So in Python, we need a simple function that approximates random error/noise"
" contributions $\\varepsilon$ drawn from a discrete Gaussian distribution "
"$\\chi$ with standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi dalam Python, kita membutuhkan fungsi sederhana yang mendekati "
"kontribusi kesalahan/noise acak $\\varepsilon$ yang ditarik dari distribusi "
"Gaussian diskret $\\chi$ dengan standar deviasi $\\sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some example values are printed so that you can see the distribution around "
"0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa nilai contoh dicetak sehingga kamu bisa melihat distribusi di "
"sekitar 0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, Alice needs to generate her key pair.\n"
msgstr "Selanjutnya, Alice perlu menghasilkan pasangan kuncinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She sets up her **private key** by choosing $n$ values between 0 and $q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dia menyiapkan **kunci privatnya** dengan memilih $n$ nilai antara 0 dan "
"$q$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice now sets up her **public key**, by choosing random vectors, which are "
"then combined with the generated errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice sekarang menyiapkan **kunci publiknya**, dengan memilih vektor acak, "
"yang kemudian dikombinasikan dengan kesalahan yang dihasilkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematika\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "More precisely, she needs to generate the sample $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"
msgstr "Lebih tepatnya, dia perlu menghasilkan sampel $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Accordingly, she randomly chooses vectors $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ and errors $\\varepsilon$ from $\\chi$ to construct $N$"
" samples $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh karena itu, dia secara acak memilih vektor $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ dan kesalahan $\\varepsilon$ dari $\\chi$ untuk "
"membangun $N$ sampel $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now share her public key.\n"
msgstr "Alice sekarang bisa berbagi kunci publiknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob can now use this to send Alice an encrypted message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob sekarang bisa menggunakan ini untuk mengirim pesan terenkripsi ke "
"Alice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's message is a single bit.\n"
msgstr "Pesan Bob adalah satu bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To encrypt the message, Bob needs to select an arbitrary number of samples "
"at random from Alice's public key to form the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengenkripsi pesan, Bob perlu memilih sejumlah sampel secara acak dari"
" kunci publik Alice untuk membentuk ciphertext.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this, he creates a mask, a random binary vector $r$ of length $N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk ini, dia membuat mask, vektor biner acak $r$ dengan panjang $N$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now take this mask and apply it to the relevant entry in Alice's public "
"key, calculating a sum of the values found.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang kita ambil mask ini dan menerapkannya ke entri yang relevan dalam "
"kunci publik Alice, menghitung jumlah nilai yang ditemukan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob broadcasts the ciphertext, which Alice can decrypt using her "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob menyiarkan ciphertext, yang bisa Alice dekripsi menggunakan "
"kunci privatnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since this protocol works bit by bit for encrypting longer bit strings, we "
"simply repeat the operations in a loop. The following shows a scenario where"
" Bob wishes to transfer 16 encrypted bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Karena protokol ini bekerja bit per bit untuk mengenkripsi string bit yang "
"lebih panjang, kita cukup mengulangi operasi dalam sebuah loop. Berikut ini "
"menunjukkan skenario di mana Bob ingin mentransfer 16 bit terenkripsi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Module-LWE and the CRYSTALS suite {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"
msgstr "Module-LWE dan suite CRYSTALS {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem, introduced in a simplified form "
"above and generally valid on arbitrary lattices, has been extended to "
"algebraic *rings* within the so-called [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729)"
" framework primarily to improve the efficiency of resulting cryptosystems. "
"However, the extra algebraic structure of Ring-LWE may be potentially "
"exploitable, even though no such exploits are currently known.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah learning with errors (LWE), yang diperkenalkan dalam bentuk "
"sederhana di atas dan umumnya berlaku pada lattice sewenang-wenang, telah "
"diperluas ke *ring* aljabar dalam kerangka yang disebut [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729)"
" terutama untuk meningkatkan efisiensi sistem kriptografi yang dihasilkan. "
"Namun, struktur aljabar tambahan dari Ring-LWE mungkin berpotensi dapat "
"dieksploitasi, meskipun saat ini tidak ada eksploitasi seperti itu yang "
"diketahui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two of the four finalists in NIST's QSC standardization process — namely, "
"the [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) key "
"encapsulation mechanism (KEM) and the [**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) digital signature protocol — are based "
"on structures known as <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Collection of all "
"submodules of a given module. A submodule is a subset of the module that "
"itself forms a module under the same operations. The set of all submodules "
"forms a lattice, which is a partially ordered set where any two elements "
"have a unique least upper bound and greatest lower bound.\">*module "
"lattices*</DefinitionTooltip> and the related [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua dari empat finalis dalam proses standardisasi QSC NIST — yaitu, "
"mekanisme enkapsulasi kunci (KEM) [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) dan protokol tanda tangan digital "
"[**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) — "
"didasarkan pada struktur yang dikenal sebagai <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Kumpulan semua submodul dari modul yang diberikan. Submodul "
"adalah subset dari modul yang sendirinya membentuk modul di bawah operasi "
"yang sama. Himpunan semua submodul membentuk lattice, yang merupakan "
"himpunan yang terurut sebagian di mana dua elemen mana pun memiliki batas "
"atas terkecil dan batas bawah terbesar yang unik.\">*lattice "
"modul*</DefinitionTooltip> dan [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090) yang terkait.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We refer interested readers to specialized courses on these topics for the "
"mathematical details but note here that Module-LWE is seen as a compromise "
"between LWE and Ring-LWE. It provides more efficiency than LWE (though less "
"than Ring-LWE) but also gives a higher level of security assurance than "
"Ring-LWE because it does not rely as heavily on the algebraic structure of "
"the problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita merujuk pembaca yang tertarik ke kursus khusus tentang topik-topik ini "
"untuk detail matematis tetapi mencatat di sini bahwa Module-LWE dipandang "
"sebagai kompromi antara LWE dan Ring-LWE. Ini memberikan lebih banyak "
"efisiensi daripada LWE (meskipun lebih sedikit daripada Ring-LWE) tetapi "
"juga memberikan tingkat jaminan keamanan yang lebih tinggi daripada Ring-LWE"
" karena tidak terlalu bergantung pada struktur aljabar masalah.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Key Encapsulation Mechanisms and CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"
msgstr ""
"Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci dan CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional asymmetric key cryptosystems are most heavily deployed for their"
" *key-exchange* and *digital signature* functionalities and as such, the "
"NIST standardization process sought to develop quantum-safe alternatives for"
" these two functionalities. The [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) protocol is therefore designed as a "
"dedicated [**Key Encapsulation "
"Mechanism**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) rather than as a general purpose encryption scheme such as RSA. A "
"workflow illustrating the use of Kyber to establish a shared secret between "
"two parties is shown below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi kunci asimetris tradisional paling banyak digunakan untuk"
" fungsionalitas *pertukaran kunci* dan *tanda tangan digital* dan karena "
"itu, proses standardisasi NIST berupaya mengembangkan alternatif quantum-"
"safe untuk kedua fungsionalitas ini. Protokol [**CRYSTALS-"
"Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) oleh karena itu "
"dirancang sebagai [**Mekanisme Enkapsulasi "
"Kunci**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) yang didedikasikan daripada sebagai skema enkripsi tujuan umum "
"seperti RSA. Alur kerja yang menggambarkan penggunaan Kyber untuk membangun "
"rahasia bersama antara dua pihak ditunjukkan di bawah ini.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"KEM example using liboqs (local setup required) {#kem-example-using-liboqs-"
"local-setup-required}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh KEM menggunakan liboqs (perlu setup lokal) {#kem-example-using-"
"liboqs-local-setup-required}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"This example requires some additional local installation, and currently cannot be run on this site. You can review the output below, or alternatively copy the cells to a suitable local environment if you wish to run these examples**\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Contoh ini memerlukan beberapa instalasi lokal tambahan, dan saat ini tidak dapat dijalankan di situs ini. Kamu bisa meninjau output di bawah ini, atau secara alternatif menyalin sel ke lingkungan lokal yang sesuai jika kamu ingin menjalankan contoh-contoh ini**\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we make use of the algorithms provided by the `liboqs` open source "
"project which provides a libraries for prototyping and experimenting with "
"quantum-safe cryptography. Refer to the links below to setup and test, and "
"then run these examples in your local Python environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kita menggunakan algoritma yang disediakan oleh proyek open source "
"`liboqs` yang menyediakan pustaka untuk membuat prototipe dan bereksperimen "
"dengan kriptografi quantum-safe. Lihat tautan di bawah ini untuk setup dan "
"pengujian, lalu jalankan contoh-contoh ini di lingkungan Python lokal "
"kamu.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Python Library:** This provides the Python language binding for liboqs - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pustaka Python:** Ini menyediakan binding bahasa Python untuk liboqs - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**liboqs implementation:** This is required by the Python library, and "
"provides the actual algorithm implementations and must be built - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\n"
msgstr ""
"**Implementasi liboqs:** Ini diperlukan oleh pustaka Python, dan menyediakan"
" implementasi algoritma aktual dan harus dibangun - https://github.com/open-"
"quantum-safe/liboqs\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to create and securely communicate a shared secret to Bob using"
" a quantum-safe encryption approach. She will use the `Kyber512` KEM "
"algorithm provided by liboqs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice ingin membuat dan mengkomunikasikan rahasia bersama kepada Bob secara "
"aman menggunakan pendekatan enkripsi quantum-safe. Dia akan menggunakan "
"algoritma KEM `Kyber512` yang disediakan oleh liboqs.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by importing relevant Python modules :\n"
msgstr "Kita mulai dengan mengimpor modul Python yang relevan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`liboqs` provides a number of KEM implementations and a list of the "
"available algorithms can be easily obtained as follows\n"
msgstr ""
"`liboqs` menyediakan sejumlah implementasi KEM dan daftar algoritma yang "
"tersedia dapat dengan mudah diperoleh sebagai berikut\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that one of the options in the list is `Kyber512` which we will employ in this example. Key exchange using Kyber involves three simple steps namely\n"
"1. Key generation\n"
"2. Encapsulation\n"
"3. Decapsulation\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahwa salah satu opsi dalam daftar adalah `Kyber512` yang akan kita gunakan dalam contoh ini. Pertukaran kunci menggunakan Kyber melibatkan tiga langkah sederhana yaitu\n"
"1. Pembuatan kunci\n"
"2. Enkapsulasi\n"
"3. Dekapsulasi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the key generation step, the recepient Bob, needs to generate an "
"asymmetric key pair using `Kyber512` and broadcast his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah pembuatan kunci, penerima Bob, perlu menghasilkan pasangan "
"kunci asimetris menggunakan `Kyber512` dan menyiarkan kunci publiknya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next in the **encapsulation** step, upon receiving Bob's public key, Alice "
"generates both the shared secret and it's corresponding ciphertext using "
"`Kyber512` and Bob's public key. The ciphertext which *encapsulates* the "
"shared secret is then broadcasted to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Selanjutnya dalam langkah **enkapsulasi**, setelah menerima kunci publik "
"Bob, Alice menghasilkan rahasia bersama dan ciphertext yang sesuai "
"menggunakan `Kyber512` dan kunci publik Bob. Ciphertext yang "
"*mengenkapsulasi* rahasia bersama kemudian disiarkan ke Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the **decapsulation** step, Bob uses his private key to recover "
"the shared secret from the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, dalam langkah **dekapsulasi**, Bob menggunakan kunci privatnya "
"untuk memulihkan rahasia bersama dari ciphertext.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that in contrast to key exchange using RSA, no extraneous padding or "
"key derivation functions are involved here. Kyber's design as a KEM allows "
"for a very minimal user interface while providing the gold standard [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security for key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa berbeda dengan pertukaran kunci menggunakan RSA, tidak ada "
"padding atau fungsi derivasi kunci yang berlebihan yang terlibat di sini. "
"Desain Kyber sebagai KEM memungkinkan antarmuka pengguna yang sangat minimal"
" sambil menyediakan standar emas keamanan [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" untuk pertukaran kunci.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IND-CPA and IND-CCA security in lattice-based cryptography {#ind-cpa-and-"
"ind-cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Keamanan IND-CPA dan IND-CCA dalam kriptografi berbasis lattice {#ind-cpa-"
"and-ind-cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the lesson on Symmetric Key Cryptography, we introduced the notion of "
"**semantic security** or **IND-CPA** security which refers to "
"[**indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext "
"attack**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran tentang Kriptografi Kunci Simetris, kita memperkenalkan "
"gagasan **keamanan semantik** atau **keamanan IND-CPA** yang mengacu pada "
"[**indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext "
"attack**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional cryptosystems whether symmetric (such as AES) or asymmetric "
"(such as RSA) use deterministic functions to implement encryption "
"operations. This means that a given plaintext, combined with a given "
"encryption key will always encrypt to the same ciphertext. Such "
"deterministic cryptosystems are vulnerable to *chosen plaintext attack* "
"whereby an adversary is able to extract information by requesting "
"encryptions of arbitrary plaintexts of their choice from the deterministic "
"encryption function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi tradisional baik simetris (seperti AES) maupun asimetris "
"(seperti RSA) menggunakan fungsi deterministik untuk mengimplementasikan "
"operasi enkripsi. Ini berarti bahwa plaintext tertentu, dikombinasikan "
"dengan kunci enkripsi tertentu, akan selalu mengenkripsi ke ciphertext yang "
"sama. Sistem kriptografi deterministik seperti itu rentan terhadap *chosen "
"plaintext attack* di mana adversary dapat mengekstrak informasi dengan "
"meminta enkripsi plaintext sewenang-wenang pilihannya dari fungsi enkripsi "
"deterministik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve IND-CPA security in this context, **additional randomness** is "
"introduced at encryption time either through *initialization vectors* or "
"*padding*. For instance AES is only IND-CPA secure when used in [Cipher "
"Block Chaining (CBC) or Gaolis/Counter Mode (GCM) modes of "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" that use random initialization vectors. Similarly with RSA, [OAEP "
"padding](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" is need to ensure IND-CPA security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mencapai keamanan IND-CPA dalam konteks ini, **keacakan tambahan** "
"diperkenalkan pada saat enkripsi baik melalui *initialization vector* maupun"
" *padding*. Misalnya AES hanya aman IND-CPA ketika digunakan dalam [mode "
"operasi Cipher Block Chaining (CBC) atau Gaolis/Counter Mode "
"(GCM)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" yang menggunakan initialization vector acak. Demikian pula dengan RSA, "
"[padding "
"OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" diperlukan untuk memastikan keamanan IND-CPA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, lattice-based schemes for encryption are inherently randomized due to the problem definition itself. In particular, in the LWE based encryption scheme outlined above, there are two distinct elements of randomness:\n"
"- **(1)** The error (or noise) $\\varepsilon$ drawn from the distribution $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ used for encrypting each bit in the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, skema berbasis lattice untuk enkripsi secara inheren teracak karena definisi masalah itu sendiri. Secara khusus, dalam skema enkripsi berbasis LWE yang diuraikan di atas, ada dua elemen keacakan yang berbeda:\n"
"- **(1)** Kesalahan (atau noise) $\\varepsilon$ yang ditarik dari distribusi $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** Vektor biner acak $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ yang digunakan untuk mengenkripsi setiap bit dalam pesan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The errors $\\varepsilon$ contribute to the security of the public key, "
"ensuring that it's computationally hard to deduce the secret key "
"$\\mathbf{s}$. The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r}$ on the other hand "
"provide the essential randomness needed for making repeated encryptions of "
"the same plaintext bit non-deterministic. Thus LWE based schemes are "
"considered IND-CPA secure without the need for external mechanisms such as "
"padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kesalahan $\\varepsilon$ berkontribusi pada keamanan kunci publik, "
"memastikan bahwa secara komputasional sulit untuk mendeduksi kunci rahasia "
"$\\mathbf{s}$. Vektor biner acak $\\mathbf{r}$ di sisi lain memberikan "
"keacakan esensial yang diperlukan untuk membuat enkripsi berulang dari bit "
"plaintext yang sama menjadi non-deterministik. Dengan demikian skema "
"berbasis LWE dianggap aman IND-CPA tanpa memerlukan mekanisme eksternal "
"seperti padding.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern cryptosystems aim to achieve so called [**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security which stands for **indistinguishability under chosen-ciphertext "
"attack**. In this setting the adversary has the ability to obtain "
"decryptions of a non-trival set of ciphertexts of their choosing with the "
"aim of extracting information to subsequently break the cryptosystem. A "
"scheme is IND-CCA secure if, even with this capability, the adversary cannot"
" do better than random guessing when trying to distinguish encrypted "
"messages. IND-CCA is a stronger security notion than IND-CPA and subsumes "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi modern bertujuan untuk mencapai apa yang disebut keamanan"
" [**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" yang merupakan singkatan dari **indistinguishability under chosen-"
"ciphertext attack**. Dalam pengaturan ini, adversary memiliki kemampuan "
"untuk mendapatkan dekripsi dari sekumpulan non-trivial ciphertext pilihannya"
" dengan tujuan mengekstrak informasi untuk kemudian memecahkan sistem "
"kriptografi. Suatu skema bersifat aman IND-CCA jika, bahkan dengan kemampuan"
" ini, adversary tidak dapat berbuat lebih baik dari menebak secara acak saat"
" mencoba membedakan pesan terenkripsi. IND-CCA adalah gagasan keamanan yang "
"lebih kuat dari IND-CPA dan mencakupnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum safe KEMs such as **Kyber** are designed to be IND-CCA secure. This is achieved in two steps:\n"
"1. An IND-CPA secure public key encryption(PKE) scheme is defined. In the case of Kyber such a PKE is based on **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. A variant of the [Fujisaki-Okamoto transform](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) is applied to obtain a CCA-secure KEM. The FO transformation is a generic method to convert encryption schemes that are IND-CPA secure into ones that are IND-CCA secure. For details we refer readers to the [original papers](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"
msgstr ""
"KEM quantum-safe seperti **Kyber** dirancang untuk bersifat aman IND-CCA. Ini dicapai dalam dua langkah:\n"
"1. Skema enkripsi kunci publik (PKE) yang aman IND-CPA didefinisikan. Dalam kasus Kyber, PKE tersebut didasarkan pada **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. Varian dari [transformasi Fujisaki-Okamoto](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) diterapkan untuk mendapatkan KEM yang aman CCA. Transformasi FO adalah metode generik untuk mengkonversi skema enkripsi yang aman IND-CPA menjadi yang aman IND-CCA. Untuk detail kita merujuk pembaca ke [makalah asli](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more information on the security features of **Kyber** and "
"**Dilithium**, as well as reference implementations in various programming "
"languages, you are encouraged to consult the [CRYSTALS suite "
"documentation](https://pq-crystals.org/).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk informasi lebih lanjut tentang fitur keamanan **Kyber** dan "
"**Dilithium**, serta implementasi referensi dalam berbagai bahasa "
"pemrograman, kamu didorong untuk berkonsultasi dengan [dokumentasi suite "
"CRYSTALS](https://pq-crystals.org/).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hybrid cryptography {#hybrid-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi hibrida {#hybrid-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hybrid cryptography refers to using quantum-safe public-key algorithms are "
"combined with traditional public key algorithms (like RSA or elliptic "
"curves) such that the solution is at least no less secure than existing "
"traditional cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi hibrida mengacu pada penggunaan algoritma kunci publik quantum-"
"safe yang dikombinasikan dengan algoritma kunci publik tradisional (seperti "
"RSA atau kurva eliptik) sedemikian rupa sehingga solusinya setidaknya tidak "
"kurang aman dari kriptografi tradisional yang ada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This can help address 2 issues:\n"
msgstr "Ini dapat membantu mengatasi 2 masalah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Existing standards may mandate specific algorithms to be used for "
"encryption, or that such algorithms are in some way approved. To add quantum"
" safety, encryption could first be done using the regular algorithm, but "
"then further protected by a quantum-safe algorithm, whilst still meeting "
"required standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Standar yang ada mungkin mengamanatkan algoritma tertentu yang digunakan "
"untuk enkripsi, atau bahwa algoritma tersebut disetujui dengan cara "
"tertentu. Untuk menambahkan keamanan kuantum, enkripsi bisa dilakukan "
"pertama menggunakan algoritma reguler, tetapi kemudian dilindungi lebih "
"lanjut oleh algoritma quantum-safe, sambil tetap memenuhi standar yang "
"diperlukan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms are new, and further analysis is needed to ensure they "
"are indeed safe and correct. For example one of the initial algorithms "
"shortlisted by NIST was subsequently cracked and proven to be insecure. To "
"mitigate this risk, encryption can be done both using a standard, well-"
"reviewed, secure (apart from quantum!) algorithm, in addition to a post-"
"quantum algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum baru, dan analisis lebih lanjut diperlukan untuk "
"memastikan bahwa algoritma tersebut memang aman dan benar. Misalnya salah "
"satu algoritma yang awalnya masuk daftar pendek oleh NIST kemudian "
"dipecahkan dan terbukti tidak aman. Untuk memitigasi risiko ini, enkripsi "
"dapat dilakukan baik menggunakan algoritma standar yang ditinjau dengan "
"baik, aman (kecuali dari kuantum!) sebagai tambahan dari algoritma post-"
"quantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The migration to quantum-safe cryptography (QSC) of asymmetric key "
"cryptosystems is necessitated by the expected advent of quantum computers "
"that can break traditional asymmetric key algorithms predicated on the "
"classical hardness of NP-intermediate problems. QSC is conjectured to be "
"robust to quantum attacks because its security is based on NP-hard problems,"
" which generally cannot be efficiently solved even with quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Migrasi ke kriptografi quantum-safe (QSC) dari sistem kriptografi kunci "
"asimetris dimandatkan oleh munculnya komputer kuantum yang diharapkan dapat "
"memecahkan algoritma kunci asimetris tradisional yang didasarkan pada "
"kesulitan klasikal dari masalah NP-intermediate. QSC diperkirakan bersifat "
"robust terhadap serangan kuantum karena keamanannya didasarkan pada masalah "
"NP-hard, yang umumnya tidak dapat diselesaikan secara efisien bahkan dengan "
"komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this context, hard problems rooted in the theory of mathematical lattices"
" such as the learning with errors (LWE) problem have emerged as leading "
"contenders for QSC standardization. In particular, the CRYSTALS-Kyber and "
"CRYSTALS-Dilithium algorithms, based on modular lattices, are well "
"positioned as near-term alternatives to popular asymmetric key protocols "
"like RSA, Elliptic Curve, Diffie-Hellman, and DSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks ini, masalah-masalah sulit yang berakar pada teori lattice "
"matematika seperti masalah learning with errors (LWE) telah muncul sebagai "
"kandidat utama untuk standardisasi QSC. Secara khusus, algoritma CRYSTALS-"
"Kyber dan CRYSTALS-Dilithium, yang didasarkan pada lattice modular, berada "
"dalam posisi yang baik sebagai alternatif jangka dekat untuk protokol kunci "
"asimetris populer seperti RSA, Elliptic Curve, Diffie-Hellman, dan DSA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we navigate the complex landscape of quantum-safe cryptography, embracing"
" these innovative solutions will be pivotal in upholding the integrity and "
"confidentiality of our digital interactions in the quantum era.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat kita menavigasi lanskap kriptografi quantum-safe yang kompleks, "
"merangkul solusi inovatif ini akan sangat penting dalam menjunjung "
"integritas dan kerahasiaan interaksi digital kita di era kuantum.\n"
